  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HPN - Kenya Conference of Catholic Bishops(KCCB) - Komesha TB program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Kenya):  USAID will utilize FY 2022 funds to invest in the Komesha Tuberculosis activity which provides county level support for the faith-based sector to reduce tuberculosis (TB) incidence and deaths. The activity will identify and empower community actors, stakeholders and TB champions to screen and refer presumptive TB cases to health facilities and will utilize faith-based media outlets and dialogue platforms to promote adherence to TB related services. The activity will collaborate with county health management teams to strengthen the capacity of faith-based health facilities to provide TB prevention, diagnosis, care and treatment services. The activity works with the National TB Programme and county teams and engages a variety of public and non-public stakeholders in development of annual county/sub-county TB work plans. The activity also expands GeneXpert networking through sensitization, specimen referral and external quality assurance to promptly identify new TB patients and place them immediately on TB treatment, hence reducing TB mortalities. Infectious disease prevention, detection and response is a priority for the U.S. security concerns as such diseases would otherwise spread beyond Kenya&apos;s borders. .</narrative>
  </description>
